river|watercourse|NOUN|large flowing watercourse|A natural stream of water that flows through land towards another body of water.|sông|The footpath follows the river past the old mill.|Lối đi bộ men theo con sông qua nhà máy xay cũ.|Countable; rivers normally flow into another river, a lake, or the sea rather than being still water.|0
to|destination|PREPOSITION|towards and reaching a destination|Used to identify the destination of a movement or journey.|đến; tới|We walked to the station before sunrise.|Chúng tôi đi bộ đến nhà ga trước khi mặt trời mọc.|Preposition followed by a destination noun phrase; this record does not treat the infinitive marker as a preposition.|0
willing|ready-without-force|ADJECTIVE|ready to do something|Ready to do something because you choose to, rather than because you are forced.|sẵn lòng|She is willing to help with the evening class.|Cô ấy sẵn lòng giúp lớp học buổi tối.|Willing to plus an infinitive names the chosen action; readiness does not guarantee ability.|0
accomplishment|achievement|NOUN|something successfully achieved|Something achieved through effort or skill, especially something worth being pleased about.|thành tựu; việc đạt được nhờ nỗ lực|Finishing the village trail was a major accomplishment for the volunteers.|Hoàn thành đường mòn của làng là một thành tựu lớn của các tình nguyện viên.|Countable for an achievement; not every accomplishment requires an award or public recognition.|0
fortunate|lucky|ADJECTIVE|having good luck|Having good luck or receiving an advantage through favourable circumstances.|may mắn|We were fortunate to find a room before the rain started.|Chúng tôi may mắn tìm được phòng trước khi trời bắt đầu mưa.|Fortunate to do something or fortunate that a situation occurs; does not necessarily describe wealth.|0
